===Etymology===
1890, from {{etyl|de}} {{term|Wurst|lang=de}} "sausage, wurst" from {{etyl|gmh}} {{term|wurst|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh}} {{term|wurst|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|wurstiz||something turned or twisted|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|wert-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|-d-||to turn|lang=ine-pro}}. Akin to {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term|worst|lang=osx}} "wurst", {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|weorþan|lang=ang}} "to turn, become". More at [[worth]].

